Let `rules_ts` source TypeScript from an existing `node_modules` tree.

`rules_ts` downloads its own copy of TypeScript into `@npm_typescript` and links every one of
the 20 platform-specific native packages unconditionally, where `rules_js` has already resolved
exactly one via `select()` over `@aspect_rules_js//platforms/pnpm:*`. That costs 20 tarball
downloads in the repository rule plus 20 `CopyDirectory` actions, for platforms that can never
execute, and duplicates a package the lockfile already provides.

Adds an `npm_package` attribute to the `typescript.deps` tag. When set, the repository rule skips
the download and the native-package linking entirely and points `tsc`, `tsc_worker` and
`validator` at the supplied label. The version attributes are still used, for the
`is_typescript_5_or_greater` config setting.

Prototype for upstreaming; relates to https://github.com/aspect-build/rules_ts/issues/787 where
the extension's fetch-its-own-copy design is already noted as misuse-prone.

